'''''Lathyrus ochrus''''', the '''Cyprus vetch''', is a species of annual herb in the family [[Fabaceae]]. They are climbers and have compound, broad leaves. Flowers are visited by [[Old World swallowtail]]s and ''[[Oxythyrea funesta]]''.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Lathyrus ochrus (L.)DC. - Encyclopedia of Life|url=https://eol.org/pages/703178|access-date=2022-02-04|website=eol.org}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Mifsud |first=Stephen |date=2002-08-23 |title=Lathyrus ochrus (Pale Pea) : MaltaWildPlants.com - the online Flora of the Maltese Islands. |url=https://www.maltawildplants.com/FABC/Lathyrus_ochrus.php |access-date=2022-03-05 |website=www.maltawildplants.com |language=en-us}}</ref>

